{"id": "EUVD-2026-95908", "enisaUuid": "ebd21885-6361-3867-bc25-79b232d2a603", "description": "AstronRPA through 1.1.6 contains a download of code without integrity check vulnerability that allows network attackers to deliver malicious updates by abusing the desktop client's auto-update mechanism. Attackers positioned between the client and server can serve a malicious update manifest and NSIS installer, which electron-updater installs without signature verification, executing code as the desktop user.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T16:04:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T19:35:24", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/issues/894", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/blob/8b015bc1b15d23fbdc55c78ff1de9af4bb65fba6/frontend/packages/electron-app/electron-builder.json#L26", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/astronrpa-through-1.1.6-unsigned-update-installation-via-plain-http-feed"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mj3v-h93p-hj6p", "CVE-2026-108160"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5951f90f-be11-3f34-8242-4cb47f5242f9", "product": {"name": "astron-rpa", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.1.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f0fd9703-40bb-3115-aa07-499cabe0f8c0", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}], "isExploited": false}